  "why": "The statement asks for an element in at least half the sets of every (finite) union-closed family, so constant-fraction results below 1/2 are bounds (F4), and restricted classes (height at most four, chains of at most three sets, ideal families, small smallest set, dense families) are cases. Within the window the live full-proof claims (Demontis, Reed, the ResearchGate paper) are not_credible: each has no uptake on a landmark problem, later papers in the window still call the conjecture open, and each has its own aggravating signal (Reed's displayed Lean theorem is trivial, and the ResearchGate claim describes its own scope inconsistently). Blinovsky–Speranca and Agama are dated by first posting because their window revisions show no new mathematics. Colbert counts as digested because Order accepted it. Jiang's AI credit is the close call. The quote 'GPT-6 Astra served as an AI assistant in the research and preparation of this manuscript' does not say the model produced any argument, construction or bound, and the record finds no statement attributing the theorem or the interval program to it. Read on the quote alone, that is too thin to be mathematics in the result, so ai_role is none. Jiang is also marked doubtful because it gives the same eight-digit constant a day after Costa–Sadhu.",
